(2607736, 361346, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the composition and the fade to black is excellent.  I tend to like a deeper DOF and in this case I''m not sure what the slightly OOF blouse is adding.  Since this is the first shot I''ve seen, I''ll likely be back to change the vote a bit. 7 for now.</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the composition and the fade to black is excellent.  I tend to like a deeper DOF and in this case I''m not sure what the slightly OOF blouse is adding.  Since this is the first shot I''ve seen, I''ll likely be back to change the vote a bit. 7 for now.', '2006-07-10 16:22:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607746, 360100, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the flipped canvas.  It adds to the abstract nature and makes it about the geometry.  The color is a bit flat, especially the background.  I would have tried for something else.  Either brighter or another color altogether. 6</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the flipped canvas.  It adds to the abstract nature and makes it about the geometry.  The color is a bit flat, especially the background.  I would have tried for something else.  Either brighter or another color altogether. 6', '2006-07-10 16:24:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607749, 361104, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the composition.  Small things to change: the blown sky and the weedy thing at center bottom (my eye keeps being drawn to it).  The B&amp;W conversion is nice.  The pic tells a story as well (always good).6</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I like the composition.  Small things to change: the blown sky and the weedy thing at center bottom (my eye keeps being drawn to it).  The B&W conversion is nice.  The pic tells a story as well (always good).6', '2006-07-10 16:26:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607757, 360022, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I think it was a creative attempt, but in the end the picture fails to capture us.  The blue tones of the sky give us a nice impression of dawn, but the rest of the picture is too murky and muddy.  The flashlight also could have been pointed at the 10 since that is the "subject".  Although I''m giving this a 4, I encourage your creative approach.</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I think it was a creative attempt, but in the end the picture fails to capture us.  The blue tones of the sky give us a nice impression of dawn, but the rest of the picture is too murky and muddy.  The flashlight also could have been pointed at the 10 since that is the "subject".  Although I''m giving this a 4, I encourage your creative approach.', '2006-07-10 16:29:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607761, 361286, 58469, '<td valign="top">Can''t vote on this one, but I think this is hilarious. It would''ve got a good score from me! <br/> <br/>Just a thought. In an attempt to be helpful, the only thing I''m not sure I like in this photo is the red background. Perhaps a dark blue sky color would have worked?</td>', 'Can''t vote on this one, but I think this is hilarious. It would''ve got a good score from me!  Just a thought. In an attempt to be helpful, the only thing I''m not sure I like in this photo is the red background. Perhaps a dark blue sky color would have worked?', '2006-07-10 16:30:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607765, 361168, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...The B&amp;W conversion and sharpness in the hands is excellent.  I typically don''t like pictures that rely on writing to convey the meaning, but this isn''t bad (as far as that goes).  The cleavage made me laugh at first, but then the connection to the "she''s a 10" dawned on me (with the title).  Even though you would need the speakers to go to your ears in real life, I wouldn''t have included them.  They look unappealing with the blurriness. 6</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...The B&W conversion and sharpness in the hands is excellent.  I typically don''t like pictures that rely on writing to convey the meaning, but this isn''t bad (as far as that goes).  The cleavage made me laugh at first, but then the connection to the "she''s a 10" dawned on me (with the title).  Even though you would need the speakers to go to your ears in real life, I wouldn''t have included them.  They look unappealing with the blurriness. 6', '2006-07-10 16:31:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607774, 360281, 58469, '<td valign="top">Awesome photo! I wish I could vote on it. I think the DOF on the feet and eyelashes is excellent. Only thing I would think might help would be to remove the veil or fabric that seems to be in the image. But, I''d have to see it without it to know one way or the other.</td>', 'Awesome photo! I wish I could vote on it. I think the DOF on the feet and eyelashes is excellent. Only thing I would think might help would be to remove the veil or fabric that seems to be in the image. But, I''d have to see it without it to know one way or the other.', '2006-07-10 16:34:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607775, 359348, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I sense the DNMC voters smell blood in the water.  With that aside, the picture has very flat lighting or a cast to it.  I think that pulls the entire picture down.  Sharpness and composition are well done.  Were it possible (and I know how fast these shots need to be taken), I would have moved to my right to get more of the fawn''s head.  I''m going to give it a 4 mainly for the flat lighting and the fact that outside the title I wouldn''t have felt "10" at all.</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...I sense the DNMC voters smell blood in the water.  With that aside, the picture has very flat lighting or a cast to it.  I think that pulls the entire picture down.  Sharpness and composition are well done.  Were it possible (and I know how fast these shots need to be taken), I would have moved to my right to get more of the fawn''s head.  I''m going to give it a 4 mainly for the flat lighting and the fact that outside the title I wouldn''t have felt "10" at all.', '2006-07-10 16:34:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607781, 361139, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...Excellently done.  I like the background which looks like a large wave poised to crash down.  The composition is well done, the focus is spot on and the lighting is dynamic.  The applicability to the topic is somewhat of a stretch, but that will only cost you a little. (by that I mean without the title I would be lost) 7</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...Excellently done.  I like the background which looks like a large wave poised to crash down.  The composition is well done, the focus is spot on and the lighting is dynamic.  The applicability to the topic is somewhat of a stretch, but that will only cost you a little. (by that I mean without the title I would be lost) 7', '2006-07-10 16:37:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607791, 361086, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...you know, I''m not really a "boy" in the sense that I get into guns or war machines, but I have always loved the Warthog.  Don''t ask me why.  This is very well captured.  Perhaps PP could have lightened up the fuselage, but no biggie.  The worst PP boo-boo (and this is small) is the bit on the left engine.  It now looks like it is "behind" the wing with the one section where it juxtaposes being altered).  I''m sure the 3-5 seconds you typically get will keep that well hidden. 7</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...you know, I''m not really a "boy" in the sense that I get into guns or war machines, but I have always loved the Warthog.  Don''t ask me why.  This is very well captured.  Perhaps PP could have lightened up the fuselage, but no biggie.  The worst PP boo-boo (and this is small) is the bit on the left engine.  It now looks like it is "behind" the wing with the one section where it juxtaposes being altered).  I''m sure the 3-5 seconds you typically get will keep that well hidden. 7', '2006-07-10 16:41:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607795, 361349, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...the capture is techincally well done.  You capture a nice motion blur while keeping the subject very sharp.  Kudos for that.  The lighting is nicely done in the morning or evening.  The composition is nice, although if I could really change anything I don''t like the trees.  They don''t appeal to me with their semi-sillouette. 7</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...the capture is techincally well done.  You capture a nice motion blur while keeping the subject very sharp.  Kudos for that.  The lighting is nicely done in the morning or evening.  The composition is nice, although if I could really change anything I don''t like the trees.  They don''t appeal to me with their semi-sillouette. 7', '2006-07-10 16:43:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607800, 359603, 33352, '<td valign="top">Nice concept</td>', 'Nice concept', '2006-07-10 16:44:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607802, 361330, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...what made you flip the starfish this way?  There is more to see, but I''m not sure if it''s more appealing or not.  The sand is just slightly blown on the left (we are starting to lose detail).  I like the composition.  Centered works here.  The starfish look just a bit bright here too.  Nicely done though. 7</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...what made you flip the starfish this way?  There is more to see, but I''m not sure if it''s more appealing or not.  The sand is just slightly blown on the left (we are starting to lose detail).  I like the composition.  Centered works here.  The starfish look just a bit bright here too.  Nicely done though. 7', '2006-07-10 16:45:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607804, 360588, 33352, '<td valign="top">Looked at this and thought this says ten ???</td>', 'Looked at this and thought this says ten ???', '2006-07-10 16:45:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607806, 359077, 33352, '<td valign="top">Colorful, amazing arrangement....</td>', 'Colorful, amazing arrangement....', '2006-07-10 16:46:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607807, 360166, 56658, '<td valign="top">whats funny is that by burning that 10 bucks you wasted less money on your shot than I did on mine:) I like the idea here. I would like to see more smoke or less of it. as it is it seems kinda distracting. 7</td>', 'whats funny is that by burning that 10 bucks you wasted less money on your shot than I did on mine:) I like the idea here. I would like to see more smoke or less of it. as it is it seems kinda distracting. 7', '2006-07-10 16:46:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607810, 360529, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...there are a few issues here.  The biggest is the soft focus, espcially on the horizontal portion of the flower.  There also seems to be either a cast or something with the lighting.  Actually I think I''ve noticed that leaves like this tend to go cyan quickly, and I don''t like that.  Did you boost saturation a ton?  that might be the problem.  Composition is fairly centered.  I''m going to give this a 4.  Work on the details above for your next entry and I bet it will do much better.</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...there are a few issues here.  The biggest is the soft focus, espcially on the horizontal portion of the flower.  There also seems to be either a cast or something with the lighting.  Actually I think I''ve noticed that leaves like this tend to go cyan quickly, and I don''t like that.  Did you boost saturation a ton?  that might be the problem.  Composition is fairly centered.  I''m going to give this a 4.  Work on the details above for your next entry and I bet it will do much better.', '2006-07-10 16:48:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607817, 361161, 33352, '<td valign="top">Has good impact...</td>', 'Has good impact...', '2006-07-10 16:49:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607818, 360999, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...boy not everybody is going to see those 10s.  The picture has very cool tones and I think I wish they were warmer.  Composition isn''t bad, although I would have tried to include the "1" in the largest ten. 5</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...boy not everybody is going to see those 10s.  The picture has very cool tones and I think I wish they were warmer.  Composition isn''t bad, although I would have tried to include the "1" in the largest ten. 5', '2006-07-10 16:49:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607824, 359957, 40718, '<td valign="top">On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...very clever.  Could you have used even more DOF to get the rim of the bowl in sharp focus?  The highlights look under control, but just barely. 7</td>', 'On the first 15 pictures I see, I''m looking for a full 30 seconds and leaving a comment...very clever.  Could you have used even more DOF to get the rim of the bowl in sharp focus?  The highlights look under control, but just barely. 7', '2006-07-10 16:51:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607826, 360197, 33352, '<td valign="top">Very graphic...and a lot of processing..</td>', 'Very graphic...and a lot of processing..', '2006-07-10 16:51:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607831, 360725, 33352, '<td valign="top">A lot to take in,very busy....</td>', 'A lot to take in,very busy....', '2006-07-10 16:54:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2607833, 361239, 56658, '<td valign="top">The subject matter is not terrible interesting to me but the processing really helps it. I might have cropped a little off the bottom. overall nice photo.</td>', 'The subject matter is not terrible interesting to me but the processing really helps it. I might have cropped a little off the bottom. overall nice photo.', '2006-07-10 16:54:42.000000', NULL, 1),
