(2624758, 360206, 50695, '<td valign="top">I just love how space is divided into three sections here, one on top and two on the bottom. On one side, people remain at the window, on the surface. on the other side people go into the door, into the depths. A seemingly arbitrary crop becomes exact. 8</td>', 'I just love how space is divided into three sections here, one on top and two on the bottom. On one side, people remain at the window, on the surface. on the other side people go into the door, into the depths. A seemingly arbitrary crop becomes exact. 8', '2006-07-15 14:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2624763, 360961, 36914, '<td valign="top">Only until the shot was done. The reflection in the upper right pulls the eys away from the subject.  Good idea and use of challenge</td>', 'Only until the shot was done. The reflection in the upper right pulls the eys away from the subject.  Good idea and use of challenge', '2006-07-15 14:30:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2624765, 359952, 36914, '<td valign="top">Nice, like the way sepia was used to enhance the droplets.</td>', 'Nice, like the way sepia was used to enhance the droplets.', '2006-07-15 14:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2624766, 359410, 50695, '<td valign="top">good decision to line the pilings up with the horizon. they seem to be holding up the sky, which is almost blank but actually has a puffy texture to it. the overall effect is quite surreal and switches visually. sometimes we see the pilings, sometimes they turn into a check pattern with the ground behind them. sometimes the foreground seems to be the subject. sometimes we can glimpse the landscape and forget the pilings are there, but just for a moment. I love this sort of visual epilepsy. 9</td>', 'good decision to line the pilings up with the horizon. they seem to be holding up the sky, which is almost blank but actually has a puffy texture to it. the overall effect is quite surreal and switches visually. sometimes we see the pilings, sometimes they turn into a check pattern with the ground behind them. sometimes the foreground seems to be the subject. sometimes we can glimpse the landscape and forget the pilings are there, but just for a moment. I love this sort of visual epilepsy. 9', '2006-07-15 14:32:22.000000', NULL, 1),
