(2627827, 360941, 31403, '<td valign="top">all of those nice horizontal and vertical lines would have served your composition better forming angles against the edges of your frame - I think you worked at getting a nice symmetrical reflection - I appreciate that - but it''s overall kind of just a snapshot because there''s not much interesting here - that''s why I say tilting your camera to make angles would help - that and get in there closer to your 10 - fill the frame with your subject so we don''t wonder what the photo is really about - <br/> <br/>You get the longest comment of the challenge - I would guess this isn''t doing so well, and I wanted to give you some input on my thoughts - hope that''s helpful.</td>', 'all of those nice horizontal and vertical lines would have served your composition better forming angles against the edges of your frame - I think you worked at getting a nice symmetrical reflection - I appreciate that - but it''s overall kind of just a snapshot because there''s not much interesting here - that''s why I say tilting your camera to make angles would help - that and get in there closer to your 10 - fill the frame with your subject so we don''t wonder what the photo is really about -  You get the longest comment of the challenge - I would guess this isn''t doing so well, and I wanted to give you some input on my thoughts - hope that''s helpful.', '2006-07-16 22:04:15.000000', NULL, 1),
