(2628770, 359354, 41337, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this got so few comments and the low score. I''m guessing the foggy glass was the issue here. Most glass shots I''ve seen that has that tonal range to die for is lit from the back as in bounced off the back wall and not directly on the glass itself. Perhaps try that. <br/> <br/>Btw, the lighting on the strawberries came out very well and I like the choices made with the background and the composition in general. This is a fairly good image. I just think maybe it got nitpicked too much.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-17 02:29:01.</i></td>', 'I''m surprised this got so few comments and the low score. I''m guessing the foggy glass was the issue here. Most glass shots I''ve seen that has that tonal range to die for is lit from the back as in bounced off the back wall and not directly on the glass itself. Perhaps try that.  Btw, the lighting on the strawberries came out very well and I like the choices made with the background and the composition in general. This is a fairly good image. I just think maybe it got nitpicked too much.', '2006-07-17 03:27:24.000000', '2006-07-17 03:29:01.000000', 0),
