(2633436, 359719, 26255, '<td valign="top">Now THAT''S funny!!! I really like this one, the composition, DOF, everything looks great.  The only thing that might have helped this one might have been to include one of those fuzzy headed trolls to show a source of the "spiked" hair.  <br/> <br/>I think a lot of voters may have voted this one down because the connection to the number 10 is not incredibly obvious (other than the 10 duckies being present).  I really like the shot, it''s just a less than ideal connection with this specific challenge.</td>', 'Now THAT''S funny!!! I really like this one, the composition, DOF, everything looks great.  The only thing that might have helped this one might have been to include one of those fuzzy headed trolls to show a source of the "spiked" hair.   I think a lot of voters may have voted this one down because the connection to the number 10 is not incredibly obvious (other than the 10 duckies being present).  I really like the shot, it''s just a less than ideal connection with this specific challenge.', '2006-07-18 16:05:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2633522, 361331, 53316, '<td valign="top">I like the concept a lot. But the card bothered me, because it was obvious from the handwriting that it was an adult, and that they were trying to mimic a child (the backwards D).  It would have been better to me to either use a child''s handwriting or just to make the D the right way so that the card would be consistant - either would be just fine.  I like how the bright colors of the card are contrasted with the rest of the shot.</td>', 'I like the concept a lot. But the card bothered me, because it was obvious from the handwriting that it was an adult, and that they were trying to mimic a child (the backwards D).  It would have been better to me to either use a child''s handwriting or just to make the D the right way so that the card would be consistant - either would be just fine.  I like how the bright colors of the card are contrasted with the rest of the shot.', '2006-07-18 17:02:18.000000', NULL, 0),
