(2643469, 361229, 41746, '<td valign="top">Being number 10 in a challenge called "The number 10" with an entry called "#10" is something you should be very proud of, Lárus. Much better than being f.ex. number 9. Even though it is apparent that you had some kind of flue during the shooting the photo is excellent. I would have given it 10 if I had voted. Congrats!</td>', 'Being number 10 in a challenge called "The number 10" with an entry called "#10" is something you should be very proud of, Lárus. Much better than being f.ex. number 9. Even though it is apparent that you had some kind of flue during the shooting the photo is excellent. I would have given it 10 if I had voted. Congrats!', '2006-07-20 19:37:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643756, 361233, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I like the creativity!  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I do remember this one from flipping through the thumbnails.  I suspect it''s rather plain as a photograph outside of the challenge, but I do like when people try stuff like this for specific challenges.  From an exposure standpoint, the black letters are a little underexposed - a tweak on levels might bring them out a bit.</td>', 'Trading Post comment I like the creativity!  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I do remember this one from flipping through the thumbnails.  I suspect it''s rather plain as a photograph outside of the challenge, but I do like when people try stuff like this for specific challenges.  From an exposure standpoint, the black letters are a little underexposed - a tweak on levels might bring them out a bit.', '2006-07-20 20:04:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643775, 361292, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Definitely meets the challenge, except the poor little 5 in the lower left, which doesn''t add with anyone to make 10.  Technically exposed and composed well, and sharp.  The part that kinda grabs your attention is trying to figure out just what the figures are on the cards - adds an interesting element!</td>', 'Trading Post comment Definitely meets the challenge, except the poor little 5 in the lower left, which doesn''t add with anyone to make 10.  Technically exposed and composed well, and sharp.  The part that kinda grabs your attention is trying to figure out just what the figures are on the cards - adds an interesting element!', '2006-07-20 20:07:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643866, 361195, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I don''t know whether this was coached or you just got lucky, but she certainly has that "I''m too sexy for my floatie device" look going for her!  A bit "snapshot centered" - some open space to the right and less on the left would create a pleasing balance (or so the photo books tell me).  I like the lighting but wish there was a tad more on her face, and I like the colors - rich and vibrant.  WAY underscored, but I suspect a lot of that was DNMC votes.  I really do like her look!</td>', 'Trading Post comment I don''t know whether this was coached or you just got lucky, but she certainly has that "I''m too sexy for my floatie device" look going for her!  A bit "snapshot centered" - some open space to the right and less on the left would create a pleasing balance (or so the photo books tell me).  I like the lighting but wish there was a tad more on her face, and I like the colors - rich and vibrant.  WAY underscored, but I suspect a lot of that was DNMC votes.  I really do like her look!', '2006-07-20 20:18:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644019, 361308, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I really like these kinds of images - simple, but seem to quietly hint there''s a story to tell (whether there really is or not.)  This one is well done.  Duotone works well here, and the focus of the image (the 10) is well placed.  Technicals are good - focus is crisp.  The shadows imply it''s about mid-day.  If you get the chance (and you''re at all interested in doing so) try reshooting this when it''s overcast to get rid of the harsh shadow, or better yet, when the shadow might be longer or at a slightly different angle.  I offer this suggestion because I''d like to see either more of the door, or less of it, going back to the "story to tell" kind of idea.</td>', 'Trading Post comment I really like these kinds of images - simple, but seem to quietly hint there''s a story to tell (whether there really is or not.)  This one is well done.  Duotone works well here, and the focus of the image (the 10) is well placed.  Technicals are good - focus is crisp.  The shadows imply it''s about mid-day.  If you get the chance (and you''re at all interested in doing so) try reshooting this when it''s overcast to get rid of the harsh shadow, or better yet, when the shadow might be longer or at a slightly different angle.  I offer this suggestion because I''d like to see either more of the door, or less of it, going back to the "story to tell" kind of idea.', '2006-07-20 20:45:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644083, 359993, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>You scumbag!  How dare you hijack Aimee''s idea!  :-)<br/> <br/>Seriously, though, this is very funny and well done.  I like the stark white background and I actually like the border, too.  I''m not always fond of borders, but I suspect this wouldn''t work without it.<br/> <br/>You stole your wife''s idea??  Heh.  Good story, though - I always enjoy reading the stories behind your pictures.</td>', 'Trading Post comment You scumbag!  How dare you hijack Aimee''s idea!  :-) Seriously, though, this is very funny and well done.  I like the stark white background and I actually like the border, too.  I''m not always fond of borders, but I suspect this wouldn''t work without it. You stole your wife''s idea??  Heh.  Good story, though - I always enjoy reading the stories behind your pictures.', '2006-07-20 21:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2645333, 361104, 19959, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi Ingibergur,<br/> <br/>Firstly, congratulations on a well deserved top 20 finish. I have looked at your portfolio and you have some excellent work there.<br/> <br/>You scored very well in this challenge but interestingly did not get a huge number of comments. DrAchoo has posted some useful feedback in that the sky and weed are the ''weak'' areas of the photo. It also seems to be a little oversharpened IMO.<br/> <br/>The conversion to black and white was a good choice for this subject and the evocative image works well and tells a story. Interesting that Pano points out that this would have worked for the perspective challenge. I see that you did enter something similar for that (so congratulations on capitialising on the location) I actually like your perspective entry a little more than this one, perhaps because of your excellent application of toning which adds a little to the shot.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a great shot. Nicely seen and executed with only small potential areas for improvement. Excellent work, I look forward to seeing more of your photos in the future.<br/> <br/>Regards Chris<br/> <br/>NOTE:<br/>It is possible to uncheck the critique option at any time during and after voting. You may find that you receive sufficient feedback through comments and your score that you may feel that you no longer require detailed critique.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi Ingibergur, Firstly, congratulations on a well deserved top 20 finish. I have looked at your portfolio and you have some excellent work there. You scored very well in this challenge but interestingly did not get a huge number of comments. DrAchoo has posted some useful feedback in that the sky and weed are the ''weak'' areas of the photo. It also seems to be a little oversharpened IMO. The conversion to black and white was a good choice for this subject and the evocative image works well and tells a story. Interesting that Pano points out that this would have worked for the perspective challenge. I see that you did enter something similar for that (so congratulations on capitialising on the location) I actually like your perspective entry a little more than this one, perhaps because of your excellent application of toning which adds a little to the shot. Overall this is a great shot. Nicely seen and executed with only small potential areas for improvement. Excellent work, I look forward to seeing more of your photos in the future. Regards Chris NOTE:It is possible to uncheck the critique option at any time during and after voting. You may find that you receive sufficient feedback through comments and your score that you may feel that you no longer require detailed critique. ', '2006-07-21 04:18:41.000000', NULL, 0),
